NAME
    make - rebuild commands from source, on-target

SYNOPSIS
    make [target]

DESCRIPTION
    A scaled-down make: it runs the pre-generated build script
    /src/mk/<target> through the same engine as `sh`. make is an OS
    built-in.

    There are no file timestamps yet (P8XFS has no mtimes), so make
    ALWAYS rebuilds -- there is no up-to-date check. Dependency
    checking can be added later.

    Targets (the scripts under /src/mk, laid down by run.sh):
      make NAME   rebuild one command (both its C and asm twins)
      make c      rebuild every C command   -> /src/commands/c/bin
      make asm    rebuild every asm command -> /src/commands/asm/bin
      make        rebuild everything (same as `make all`)

    A C command is built cc -> asm from /src/commands/c/NAME.c; a
    hand-asm command is assembled from /src/commands/asm/NAME.asm.
    The binaries land under /src/commands/{c,asm}/bin.

EXAMPLES
    make pwd
    make c
    make

SEE ALSO
    sh, cc, asm, run
